    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a14">

                <pb facs="0256" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg200"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: In reply to your letter on
                    fog-signals, &amp;c., I am of opinion that the <pb facs="0257" n="201"
                        xml:id="pg201"/> interval between, each signal, ought only to be two instead
                    of three minutes. The steering rules I have found practically to be very useful
                    in American waters, where they seem to be well understood.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES WEIR.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ismay, Imrie</hi> &amp; Co.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
